	//
	// `draft` — made, and never turned on. `live` — turned on: it can work. `paused` — stopped by
	// hand, or because its steward left the company (decision 0879 keeps that pause for an agent
	// with a role of its own); "it stops either way", and it "runs again only once someone who stays turns it
	// on". `stopped` — an agent a member built for themselves, once that member has left the
	// company: "it never runs here again". `proposed` — a turning-on or a change that is waiting
	// for approval; DECLARED AND NOT REACHED YET, because the proposal gate is a later package's.
	//
	// AN AGENT IN TRASH KEEPS THE STATE IT HAD, and is found only through the Trash's operations;
	// it comes back as a draft or paused. Its owner leaving is the one thing that moves it there, to
	// `stopped`, and then it comes back `stopped` (decision 0950). An erased agent is not found at all.
	//
	// `quarantined` — frozen under a hold until a person releases it, and then paused (ONPLO-5636):
	// "running jobs HALT and the state reads quarantined with sessions preserved under the hold". One
	// in Trash comes back quarantined. This said "QUARANTINED IS NOT IN THIS LIST: it is a later
	// package's" until then.
