	// EndChatShare End a share of a chat
	//
	// THE ACCESS STOPS AT ONCE. The share is ended and never deleted, and ending one that has
	// already ended is not an error: nothing left to end is a complete end.
	//
	// ENDED WHERE IT WAS PLACED. A chat sits in no folder, so the only access that reaches one
	// from elsewhere is a role held across the whole account environment. That is ended where it
	// was given, never here (409 `share_placed_elsewhere`). An id that names no share reaching
	// this chat is the 404, never told apart from somebody else's.
	//
	// A CHAT IN TRASH: a share of one is ended like any other, by its owner.
	//
	// ITS OWNER ENDS IT, AND SO DOES A MANAGER, as on sharing (ONPLO-2158; this said "TODAY NOBODY
	// ELSE: a Manager is answered the 404" until 12 October 2026). A Manager does not find a chat
	// in Trash (404): "nobody it was shared with reaches it there".
	//
	// When the identity service cannot be reached, 503 `identity_unavailable`: whether the share
	// ended is not known, so send the same request again.
