	// one chat (`grantable_at: both`, pull request 2174, ONPLO-1723 point 1). So the permission
	// is asked of the chat named in the path, and an owner who holds it on their own chat brings
	// it back with no role across the environment. Whichever way it is held, only the owner's own
	// chat is found: a deleted chat is reachable "to its owner until the keep-time runs out", and
	// "nobody it was shared with reaches it there". A CORRECTION, MADE IN THE OPEN: this said
	// "HELD ACROSS THE ENVIRONMENT … never on one chat … Whether a chat's owner may bring back
	// their own without that is open (ONPLO-1723, point 1)" until the catalogue ruled.
	//
	// A chat not in Trash is refused (409 `chat_not_in_trash`). One whose keep-time ran out is gone:
