// EVERY CHANGE IS KEPT. The page: "Every change is versioned (History & restore)". What the
// agent was before this change becomes a version: `GET /agents/{agent_id}/versions` lists them,
// and `POST /agents/{agent_id}/versions/{version_id}/restore` brings one back as the newest
// save. A save that changes nothing keeps nothing. This said "Reading those versions and
// restoring one are not here: no permission in the catalogue names either (ONPLO-1546, point
// 9)" until 2026-10-08, when the catalogue gave each its own (ONPLO-1870).
//
// A CHANGE TO A LIVE AGENT TAKES EFFECT AT ONCE, IN THIS SLICE. Where "needs approval" is on,
// the page sends a change through the proposal gate first; that gate is a later package's,
// and until it is built nothing waits.
//
// WHOSE IT IS CANNOT BE CHANGED HERE. An agent "belongs to where it was built".
