// DuplicateAgentWithBody Duplicate an agent
//
// "A NEW AGENT WITH THE SAME CONFIG, MADE OFF AND NEVER LIVE UNTIL IT IS TURNED ON." The new
// agent has the name and the instructions of the one in the path as it stands now — a `name`
// sent here takes the place of the first — and is a draft whatever state the original is in.
//
// WHAT IS NOT COPIED: where the original stands, its history (a new agent has no earlier
// versions), who it is shared with, the memory stores it names (naming a store asks a read of it,
// and a copy asks none), the tools it has (no tool's list names a new agent), and anything that
// points at it. The new agent is a new id,
// and nothing that used the original uses the copy.
//
// WHOSE IT BECOMES FOLLOWS BUILDING ONE (`POST /agents`), and is said in the request:
// `company` is refused in a personal environment, and `personal` asked by an agent or a machine
// (422, naming `owner_scope`). A personal copy is the caller's own, whoever built the original.
//
// THE IDENTITY SERVICE IS TOLD BEFORE THE COPY IS THERE FOR ANYBODY, as when one is built. When
// it cannot be told, nothing was made: 503 `identity_unavailable`, and the same request can be
// sent again.
//
// ASKED ABOUT THE ORIGINAL, AND TWICE: `ai:agent-copy.create`, its own act and not building an
// agent (decision 0651), and `ai:agent.read`, because the copy hands over the original's name and
// instructions (decision 0927). Each may be held across the account environment or on this one
// agent. Without both the answer is one 403, which does not say which is missing, and nothing is
// made. An agent in Trash is not duplicated here: 404.
//
// THE COPY'S USERNAME IS FILLED FROM ITS NAME, as a new agent's is when none is sent: a username
// is never copied, because no two agents here share one (ONPLO-3711). Taken in the same moment by
// another agent, it is refused: 409 `agent_username_taken`.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with POST /agents/{agent_id}/duplicate (the `DuplicateAgent` operationId).
