// ShareAgentWithBody Share an agent
//
// "Teams/members + external guests, roles Viewer/Commenter/Editor/Manager." A Viewer sees the
// agent and uses it in Chat; a Commenter holds exactly what a Viewer holds; an Editor also
// changes its setup, turns it on, pauses it, duplicates it and moves it to Trash; a Manager also
// shares it onward. The register of role definitions is where each is written (ONPLO-1974).
//
// WITH A PERSON OR A TEAM, by id. An external guest is not offered yet. Nobody by that id in this
// account environment is refused (409 `recipient_not_found`).
//
// SHARING AGAIN CHANGES THE SHARE THAT IS THERE: "ONE DIRECT GRANT PER PERSON PER OBJECT"
// (decision 0650), as for a chat and a memory store. `created` says which it was, and the status
// is `200` either way.
//
// `access_until` IS THE MOMENT THIS SHARE ENDS, as on every grant (decision 0650). One that has
// already passed is refused (422 naming `access_until`, `access_until_passed`).
//
// AN AGENT IN TRASH IS NOT FOUND HERE (404), for all three acts on its shares: it is out of use
// there (decision 0707, rule 3) and nobody it was shared with reaches it.
//
// THE IDENTITY SERVICE KEEPS THE GRANT, AND WRITES IT ITSELF. When it cannot be reached, 503
// `identity_unavailable`: whether the share landed is not known, so send the same request again.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with POST /agents/{agent_id}/grants (the `ShareAgent` operationId).
