// account environment or on one chat (`grantable_at: both`, pull request 2174, ONPLO-1723
// point 1), and only the owner's own chat is found. This said "HELD ACROSS THE ENVIRONMENT, as
// bringing one back is (ONPLO-1723, point 1)" until the catalogue ruled.
//
// THROUGH A REMOVAL, ALWAYS (decision 0648, rule 1), as an agent's delete for ever is: the chat is
// handed to the deletion service, which asks AI to erase it with its history, and AI tells the
// identity service it is gone at that erase, so every share of it ends (decision 0707). Once handed
// over it is hidden at once and cannot be brought back. A delete sent again is the same removal.
// So a legal hold sees the chat too (decision 0686). This said "THE IDENTITY SERVICE IS TOLD IT IS
// GONE, at the erase … When it cannot be told, nothing was erased: 503 `identity_unavailable`"
// and "NOT BUILT YET" until it was built (ONPLO-4652).
