// GiveJobWithBody Give a job
//
// "TYPE IT, PICK THE AGENT (OR LET ONPLO SUGGEST ONE)." What the job is, in the words of
// whoever gives it, and the agent or the machine that does it. Leave both out and the job waits
// with nobody on it, as the task service keeps a job given with "let Onplo suggest one". Who
// suggests is not built, and it suggests agents only, never a machine.
//
// IT IS MADE WAITING. Something picks it up and it runs; nothing here starts it.
//
// THE TASK SERVICE MAKES IT AND TELLS THE IDENTITY SERVICE, under the kind `ai:job`, before it
// is there for anybody (decision 0709, rule 4). When the task service cannot be reached,
// nothing was made: 503 `tasks_unavailable`, and the same request can be sent again.
//
// AN AGENT OR A MACHINE, NEVER A PERSON, RULED (decision 0723 point 2): "THE AI APP GIVES JOBS TO
// AI AGENTS ONLY", and a task for a colleague is made in Flows → Tasks. A person or a team is not
// given a job here. This said "NOT YET RULED (ONPLO-1690, point 1)" until the ruling, and "a
// machine is not given a job here" until ONPLO-3710.
//
// OR ONE OF YOUR CONNECTED MACHINES (ONPLO-3710): "One job has one doer: an agent, or a connected
// machine, never both." Name it in `machine_id`, and "Assign work to machines" (`ai:machine.run`)
// is asked of THAT machine, held on it or across the account environment. A machine you may not
// give work to answers as one that does not exist: 422, naming `machine_id`, and nothing is
// given. The job runs on that machine, on the AI subscription signed in there; an offline one may
// be named, and the job waits until it calls home. Naming both an agent and a machine is refused
// (422 `job_has_two_doers`, naming `machine_id`).
//
// THE GIVER SEES IT ALWAYS (decision 0723 point 3), with or without an agent on it: the task
// service tells identity who gave it, as the default holder of `ai:job.read` (pull request
// 2336). This said "Not yet true: identity is not told who gave it (ONPLO-1865)" until then.
//
// GIVEN "WITH APPROVAL", IT IS STILL MADE WAITING, AND THAT IS NOT YET WHAT IS RULED. Pull
// request 2174 (ONPLO-1690 point 2): a member whose giving is "with approval" gives a job that
// "opens as “waiting for approval (manager)”, and only once it is approved does it wait for an
// agent to pick it up". The task service has no move from waiting to waiting for approval
// (ONPLO-1786, the domain-shared lane's), so this cannot make one yet; the top of this
// contract says so.
// `agent_id` names an agent in this account environment, or it is refused (422, naming it).
//
// A TITLE THE TASK SERVICE STILL REFUSES IS REFUSED HERE (ONPLO-4103): 422 `job_title_refused`,
// naming `title`, and nothing is made. `JobTitle` says why none should, and why the answer stays.
//
