// WriteToMemoryStoreWithBody Write to a memory store — add, change or remove an entry
//
// HOW A WRITE LANDS IS A FIXED RULE, NEVER A SETTING. "A person with Editor rights writes LIVE
// (attributed, revertable); an AI's write becomes a PENDING item that is not retrievable until a
// Manager approves it." And "in your OWN store an AI's write lands live, attributed and
// revertable: personal scope is never gated" (decision 0250). So the answer's `state` is `live`
// or `pending`, and the caller never picks it.
//
// AN AGENT WRITES ONLY WHERE BOTH SIDES SAY YES: the store's Agent writes is on, and the
// agent's builder names the store under Memory. Otherwise 409 `agent_writes_off`.
//
// A FACT IS NEVER SILENTLY OVERWRITTEN. Changing one keeps the old entry, marked superseded by
// the new: "the price was €90 until March, €95 since".
//
// AN ENTRY IS A FACT OR A NOTE HERE. A knowledge file "gets in by being picked from Storage,
// never copied", and that reads a Storage permission this slice does not ask yet.
//
// AN AGENT'S WRITE LANDS BY WHOSE STORE IT IS. In a personal store of the agent's owner it is
// `live`: "personal scope is never gated". Anywhere else it is `pending` until the store's
// Manager approves it, and not listed until then. A machine is no agent, and its write is
// `agent_writes_off`.
//
// AN AGENT'S CHANGE OR REMOVAL WAITS THE SAME WAY, AND THE OLD ENTRY STANDS UNTIL THE OK. A
// waiting change's new entry is not listed, and the entry it changes is listed as it was; a
// waiting removal leaves the entry listed. Approving the write lands the change.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with POST /memory-stores/{memory_store_id}/writes (the `WriteToMemoryStore` operationId).
