	// ChangeChatShareWithBodyWithResponse Change a share of a chat
	//
	// A DIFFERENT ROLE, OR A DIFFERENT END. Every field is optional; an omitted field is
	// untouched, and an explicit `null` on `access_until` removes the end. A body that sets
	// neither is refused (422). Both edits land or neither does.
	//
	// CHANGED WHERE IT WAS PLACED, as a share is ended: a role held across the whole account
	// environment is changed where it was given (409 `share_placed_elsewhere`).
	//
	// A SHARE THAT HAS ENDED IS NEVER BROUGHT BACK BY CHANGING ITS END (409 `share_ended`). The
	// person is shared with again, which is `POST /chats/{chat_id}/grants` and a new share.
	//
	// A new end that has already passed is refused as on sharing (422 naming `access_until`,
	// `access_until_passed`).
	//
	// **A SHARE OF A CHAT THAT IS IN TRASH IS NOT CHANGED YET: it answers 501**, and nothing
	// changes (ONPLO-2159, point 4).
	//
	// ITS OWNER CHANGES IT, AND SO DOES A MANAGER, as on sharing (ONPLO-2158; this said "TODAY
	// NOBODY ELSE: a Manager is answered the 404" until 12 October 2026). A Manager does not find
	// a chat in Trash (404), so the 501 above is its owner's answer.
	//
	// When the identity service cannot be reached, 503 `identity_unavailable`: whether the change
	// landed is not known, so send the same request again.
