// ListAgentsWithResponse The agents you may see
//
// ONE ROW PER AGENT SOMEBODY BUILT HERE: what it is called, what it is told, whose it is, who
// answers for it, the state it is in and how its last run went. Oldest first.
//
// ONLY WHAT YOU MAY SEE. The page: "See the agents you may use". An agent is seen by whoever
// holds the permission across the account environment, and by whoever was given it on that
// one agent, so the permission is asked of each row and never at the door (decision 0693).
// One you hold nothing on is not in this list — absent, never masked. A page still holds up
// to `limit` agents, and the cursor carries on after the last one shown.
//
// THE AGENTS NOBODY BUILT ARE NOT IN THIS LIST. The built-in group — the Assistant, the Flow
// builder, the Compliance helper — is "visible, untouchable" on the page, and no page says
// what such a row is as data (ONPLO-1546, point 8).
//
// NARROWED TO WHAT WAS SHARED WITH YOU: `shared=with_me`. "Shared with me" and "Shared with
// others" are, in this app, "FILTERS on the list the objects already sit in" (the shared
// rules). With it the list holds the agents on which a share placed on that very agent reaches
// you, and none you built for yourself, in the same order, each still asked of identity. A
// role held across the whole account environment shares no agent with you.
//
// NARROWED TO WHAT YOU SHARED: `shared=with_others`. The list holds every agent on which you
// placed a share that still lives (`shareAgent`, ONPLO-5524), your own and one you shared
// onward as its Manager, in the same order, each still asked of identity. Which shares you
// placed is the identity service's to say, and this list asks it.
//
// EITHER FILTER NARROWS `owner_scope` TOO, never widens it. A cursor continues only under the
// filter it was handed out under; under another it is refused, `cursor_invalid`. This said "NO
// 'SHARED WITH ME' AND NO 'SHARED WITH OTHERS' HERE YET … no operation shares an agent" until
// sharing an agent was declared (ONPLO-2213).
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /agents (the `ListAgents` operationId).
