// DeleteAgentForEverWithResponse Delete an agent in Trash for ever
//
// "DELETE FOR EVER, ON A CHAT OR AN AGENT IN TRASH, … ASKS ONCE, and it is never an AI agent's
// to press." The agent, and every version kept of it, leave for good and cannot come back.
//
// THROUGH A REMOVAL, ALWAYS (decision 0648, rule 1): the agent is handed to the deletion
// service, which asks AI to erase it, and AI tells the identity service it is gone at that
// erase (decision 0707). Once handed over it is hidden at once and cannot be brought back. A
// delete sent again is the same removal. This said "The deletion service's intake is not built
// (ONPLO-1139)" until that intake was built.
