// PauseAgentWithResponse Pause an agent
//
// ONE ACT, AND IT IS LOGGED. A live agent becomes paused and takes no new work. It deletes
// nothing, and `POST /agents/{agent_id}/turn-on` brings it back.
//
// ALREADY PAUSED IS NOT AN ERROR. The agent is answered as it stands.
//
// WHAT IS REFUSED (409). A draft was never on, and an agent that has stopped for good cannot
// be paused back into reach.
//
// WHAT HAPPENS TO WORK IT WAS IN THE MIDDLE OF is three sentences on three pages (ONPLO-1546,
// point 1), and there is no work in this slice for it to be in the middle of.
//
// A QUARANTINED AGENT IS NOT PAUSED (409 `agent_quarantined`): only a release moves it, and it
// comes back paused. Quarantine shares this permission and is its own act,
// `POST /agents/{agent_id}/quarantine`. This said "QUARANTINE IS NOT HERE … a later package's"
// until ONPLO-5636.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
