// ShareChatWithBodyWithResponse Share a chat
//
// "SHARE A SINGLE CHAT WITH SOMEONE → IT APPEARS IN THEIR SHARED WITH ME. What they may do
// with it is the access you gave them, exactly as on any other object."
//
// ONE OF FOUR ROLES, and the Chat page says what each lets its holder do. "Viewer reads the
// exchange. Commenter reads it and comments on it, in the comments every shared object has.
// Editor carries it on, under the Editor's own access. Manager also shares it and changes who
// may reach it."
//
// WITH A PERSON. The page says "someone" and "the other person", and no page says a chat is
// shared with a team or with a guest outside the account environment (ONPLO-2159, point 1).
// So `recipient.kind` takes `person` and nothing else until one does. Nobody by that id in
// this account environment is refused (409 `recipient_not_found`).
//
// SHARING AGAIN CHANGES THE SHARE THAT IS THERE. "ONE DIRECT GRANT PER PERSON PER OBJECT"
// (decision 0650): a person holds at most one share placed on a chat. Shared with again, their
// share takes the new role and the new end and keeps its id. So the answer says which it was,
// in `created`, and the status is `200` either way: a retry after a timeout reads `false` and
// the same share, never a second one.
//
// `access_until` IS THE MOMENT THIS SHARE ENDS: "A GRANT THAT ENDS, ENDS AT A MOMENT", a date,
// a time and the time zone they were chosen in (decision 0650). It simply stops then. A moment
// that has already passed, by the service's clock, is refused (422 naming `access_until`,
// `access_until_passed`). The Chat page never mentions an end; this takes one on the
// decision's word, which is every grant's (ONPLO-2159, point 5).
//
// KEEP THE SHARE'S ID. Listing who a chat is shared with is not declared: no page says who may
// open that list (ONPLO-2159, point 2). The id answered here is what changes or ends this
// share later.
//
// NOBODY IS TOLD BY THIS CALL. AI's Notification preferences page lists no event for a chat
// shared with you (ONPLO-2159, point 3), so there is no `notify` here, as Storage's share has.
//
// A CHAT IN TRASH: "nobody it was shared with reaches it there", and no page says whether one
// can be shared while it is there (ONPLO-2159, point 4). Nothing here promises either answer:
// **sharing a chat that is in Trash is NOT BUILT YET and answers 501**, and nothing is shared.
//
// ITS OWNER SHARES IT, AND SO DOES A MANAGER. "Manager also shares it and changes who may reach
// it": a person the chat was shared with as Manager shares it as its owner does (ONPLO-2158;
// this said "that is not built: a Manager the chat was shared with is answered the 404" until
// 12 October 2026). The grant that counts is one placed on this very chat: holding the act
// across the whole account environment shares nobody's chat, and is the 404. A chat in Trash
// is not found by a Manager (404): "nobody it was shared with reaches it there", so the 501
// above is its owner's answer.
//
// NEVER AN AI AGENT'S TO DO, and never a raw key's: a share is a grant of access (403
// `ring_requires_person`).
//
// THE IDENTITY SERVICE KEEPS THE GRANT, AND WRITES IT ITSELF. When it cannot be reached, 503
// `identity_unavailable`: whether the share landed is not known, so send the same request
// again. It is the same act, and answers the share that is there. This said "nothing was
// shared" until the operation was served; identity may have written the grant before the
// answer was lost, so that was never AI's to promise.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /chats/{chat_id}/grants (the `ShareChat` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) ShareChatWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, chatId ChatId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*ShareChatResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.ShareChatWithBody(ctx, chatId, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseShareChatResponse(rsp)
}

