// ListJobsWithResponse The jobs you may see
//
// ONE ROW PER JOB: what it is, who does it and where it stands. The job that changed last
// comes first.
//
// ONLY WHAT YOU MAY SEE. "Seeing a row grants nothing on its own: a job you may watch is not a
// job you may touch." A job is seen by whoever holds the permission across the account
// environment, and by whoever was given it on that one job, so the permission is asked of
// each row and never at the door (decision 0693). One you hold nothing on is not in this list —
// absent, never masked.
//
// PERSONAL WORK IS THE JOBS YOU GAVE, AND THIS DOES NOT YET LIST ONLY THOSE. Ruled (pull
// request 2174, ONPLO-1690 point 4): "This list is the jobs YOU gave … the company's Work page
// lists every job you may read." The task service keeps who gave each task and lists them by
// assignee alone, never by who gave them; narrowing a page after it came back would answer
// short pages and a cursor that skips, so nothing here narrows it. So in a personal account
// environment as in a business one, this lists every job you may see, and `state` narrows it.
// Each row says who gave it (`given_by`). Listing only the jobs you gave waits on the task
// service's list learning to be narrowed by who gave a task — the domain-shared lane's. This
// said "WHOSE JOBS A PERSONAL WORK LIST SHOWS is not stated … (ONPLO-1690, point 4)" until the
// page ruled.
