// ClaimWorkWithBodyWithResponse Claim a job and the files it will change
//
// "A worker claims a piece of work and the folders or files it will change, before it starts."
// The caller is that worker: the job's doer, a person, an agent or a machine. Anybody else is
// refused (409 `not_the_jobs_doer`). Sent again by the same worker, the paths are replaced.
//
// ONE CLAIM PER JOB. "A second worker is refused the same piece, as a waiting job is taken by
// one doer at a time": a job has one doer, so only one worker may claim it. A claim left by a
// doer the job no longer has is replaced. A job that is done or cancelled takes no claim (409
// `job_not_open`).
//
// PREMIUM, AND WHOEVER ASKED PAYS (decision 1050): "A job a person gave counts that person's
// Premium seat when its worker claims it", and a machine user or an agent that took the work
// on its own counts its own. Without it, 409 `needs_premium`, and the job's `given_by` says
// whose seat that is.
//
// SERVED SINCE THE SERVER IMAGE HANDS AI ACCOUNT'S ANSWER ABOUT A NAMED PERSON (ONPLO-5473,
// ONPLO-5526): AI asks it whose seat counts (ONPLO-5476). This said "NOT SERVED YET" and
// answered 501 until then.
//
// THE ANSWER CARRIES THE OVERLAP WARNINGS: every other live claim that names one of the same
// files, "before either writes". A person picks who goes first; nothing here refuses an overlap.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with PUT /jobs/{job_id}/claim (the `ClaimWork` operationId).
