// ReportMachineHeartbeatWithBodyWithResponse A machine's heartbeat
//
// "Outbound poll/heartbeat/trace-stream": the connector on a machine says it is there, every 60
// seconds, with what it is running and what this month cost so far. It is what the board shows:
// presence, health, running now and the cost estimate (ONPLO-3448, point 2).
//
// A MACHINE REPORTS ON ITSELF AND ON NOTHING ELSE. It calls as itself, holding the
// machine-connector credential Integrations made when it was connected (ONPLO-4445), so the
// machine is the caller and no permission is asked: no role can give the right to say one is
// there, and none can take it away. Revoking the credential in Developer Access stops the calls.
// A person or an agent calling it is refused (403 `reported_by_a_machine_only`), and nothing is
// written.
//
// EACH HEARTBEAT REPLACES THE LAST ONE WHOLE. `running` is every job the machine works on now,
// and a job left out is no longer running here. `last_progress_at` is when that job last moved,
// which is how the board tells a stalled job from a working one. A `month_cost_estimate` of
// `null`, or left out, keeps none for this month.
//
// THE ANSWER IS THE MACHINE AS THE BOARD NOW SHOWS IT, so the connector reads `paused` there and
// takes no new job while it is `true`.
//
// AND EACH HEARTBEAT LEAVES ITS AUDIT EVENT, one a minute per machine: the baseline's "any write
// action" has no exception for presence (§3.1).
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /machine-connector/heartbeat (the `ReportMachineHeartbeat` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) ReportMachineHeartbeatWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*ReportMachineHeartbeatResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.ReportMachineHeartbeatWithBody(ctx, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseReportMachineHeartbeatResponse(rsp)
}

