// ApproveMemoryWriteWithResponse Approve an AI's write to a memory store
//
// "An AI's write becomes a PENDING item that is not retrievable until a Manager approves it."
// This is that OK: the write goes live, and its entry is answered from then on. The register's
// Manager role holds it.
//
// THE OK LANDS THE WRITE. An add's entry is listed from now on; a change supersedes the old
// entry by the new one; a removal ends the entry. When somebody changed or removed that entry
// since, the OK is refused (409 `memory_entry_not_found`), nothing is written, and the write
// still waits.
//
// Only a pending write is approved (409 `memory_write_not_pending`): not a live one, one
// approved already, or one taken back. Only a person approves, because four-eyes means the
// eyes are human: an agent or a machine is refused (403 `ring_requires_person`), and nothing
// is written. The approval is signed, `approved_by_person_id` and `approved_at`, and nothing
// else of the write moves.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /memory-stores/{memory_store_id}/writes/{write_id}/approve (the `ApproveMemoryWrite` operationId).
