// ProposeSkillReleaseWithBodyWithResponse Propose a release of a skill
//
// "Propose a release pins the current files and names who approves." The release holds the
// Storage version of each file in the skill's folder at this moment, "since a folder has no
// version of its own". It waits, proposed, until the person it names approves it.
//
// WHO APPROVES: one person, `approver_id`, who holds "Approve a skill release". In a business
// environment the proposer cannot name themselves (422 naming `approver_id`), "so every release
// has a second pair of eyes"; in a personal environment its owner names, and approves, their
// own. The approval is asked of that person in their Overview, as every ask is. An agent may
// propose a release, and a person always approves it.
//
// ONE WAITS AT A TIME: proposing again replaces a release still waiting, which is then
// `withdrawn`. A folder whose files match the live release has nothing to propose (409
// `nothing_to_release`).
//
// PREMIUM: without AI's Premium seat, 409 `needs_premium`.
//
// **NOT BUILT YET — it answers 501 (ONPLO-5345).**
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /skills/{folder_id}/releases (the `ProposeSkillRelease` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) ProposeSkillReleaseWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, folderId SkillFolderId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*ProposeSkillReleaseResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.ProposeSkillReleaseWithBody(ctx, folderId, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseProposeSkillReleaseResponse(rsp)
}

