// UpdateToolWithBodyWithResponse Set a tool's governance
//
// "Set a tool's governance — default risk tier (On its own · You review · Asks first), the
// outbound-drafts default, and which agents and people may use it." What is sent replaces what
// was there; what is left out stays.
//
// "GIVING AN AGENT A TOOL TAKES BOTH SIDES. The tool's lists decide which agents MAY have it;
// changing the agent picks from those." Naming an agent here allows it; it does not give it the
// tool. Taking an agent off the list takes the tool from it, and it says so.
//
// EACH AGENT NAMED IS ONE YOU MAY SEE: `ai:agent.read` of that agent, asked of each id in
// `agent_ids` with the act. One you may not see answers as one that does not exist: 422, naming
// `agent_ids`.
//
// THE DRAFTS DEFAULT STARTS ON. Outbound communication "defaults to drafts … until someone
// consciously changes it": turning it off is this call, and only this call.
//
// SENDING WHAT IS ALREADY THERE CHANGES NOTHING, and the tool is answered as it is.
//
// WHO MAY GIVE IT IS KEPT BY THE IDENTITY SERVICE, AS A GRANT ON THE TOOL (ONPLO-3538). Who may
// give a tool is an access fact, and every access fact is a grant the identity service keeps
// (decision 0650); Onplo stores none. Each person in `giver_person_ids` holds `ai:tool.assign`,
// placed on this tool alone, so the identity service ends it when the person is erased, leaves the
// company, or the tool is taken out. The list sent replaces the list: a person added is given the
// grant, and a person left out has it ended, each asked as you, under this operation.
//
// A PERSON THE IDENTITY SERVICE CANNOT JUDGE YET — one who is not a member of this company —
// answers 503 `identity_unavailable`, and nothing is kept: a grant this call already placed is
// ended again. A person who is not in this account environment at all is 422, naming
// `giver_person_ids`.
//
// EACH TEAM IN `giver_team_ids` HOLDS THE SAME GRANT, HELD BY THE TEAM, and the list sent replaces
// the list the same way. People and teams are two lists: sending one leaves the other as it was. A
// team the identity service does not keep in this company — deleted, another company's, or never
// made — is 422, naming `giver_team_ids`, and nothing is kept. What the team's grant lets its
// members do when they give the tool is the identity service's to answer. This answered 501 for a
// team until the identity service kept a team's grant (ONPLO-2884).
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with PATCH /tools/{tool_id} (the `UpdateTool` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) UpdateToolWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, toolId ToolId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*UpdateToolResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.UpdateToolWithBody(ctx, toolId, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseUpdateToolResponse(rsp)
}

// UpdateToolWithResponse Set a tool's governance
//
