// GiveToolToAgentWithBodyWithResponse Give a tool to an agent
//
// "Nobody uses a tool directly; a person only ever gives it to an agent."
//
// "GIVING AN AGENT A TOOL TAKES BOTH SIDES. The tool's lists decide which agents MAY have it;
// changing the agent picks from those." So two things are asked, as one question:
// `ai:tool.assign` of the tool, held by the people and teams on its list of who may give it, and
// `ai:agent.change` of the agent in the body.
//
// AN AGENT THE TOOL'S LIST DOES NOT NAME IS REFUSED, and nothing is written: 422, naming
// `agent_id`. So is an agent of another account environment.
//
// GIVING IT AGAIN CHANGES NOTHING: what is there is answered, with the moment it was first given.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /tools/{tool_id}/given-to (the `GiveToolToAgent` operationId).
